@opencut/editor-classic
Copyright 2025-2026 OpenCut

This package is built from a fork of OpenCut Classic
(https://github.com/OpenCut-app/opencut-classic), pinned at upstream commit
cf5e79e919144200294fb9fed22a222592a0aeea. The upstream MIT licence is shipped
verbatim as the LICENSE file beside this notice.

The fork (https://github.com/DumoeDss/rocut) modifies and extends the upstream
sources; the modifications in the shipped tree are recorded in the fork's
provenance set (PATCHES.md, SOURCE_INVENTORY.md, UPSTREAM.md) at the repository
root.

MV recipe drawing and selective color finishing in
src/services/renderer/programmatic/mv-recipe-{renderer,post}.ts adapt concepts
and color formulas from vocaloid-style-mv-pipeline's engine/scenes/scenes.js,
engine/scenes/meta.js, engine/core/draw.js, engine/core/trans.js and engine/core/gl.js, commit
13b380dab077d4c8ea956825c9693c720e0c2b91. The implementation is generalized for
Rocut's Rust-evaluated recipes, semantic role outputs and preserved alpha;
it does not include the upstream song, character assets or JIZURA engine.

src/services/renderer/programmatic/mv-light-leak-renderer.ts rasterizes the two
screen-gradient overlays adapted from engine/scenes/meta.js. Geometry and the
seeded clock are evaluated by Rocut's Rust recipe layer; the renderer adds an
explicit alpha-preserving option alongside the original expanding coverage.

src/services/renderer/programmatic/mv-afterimage-renderer.ts adapts the mask,
ink-centered text, five ghost rasters and grain composition from the afterimage
scene in engine/scenes/intro.js at the same reference commit. It draws only
Rust-evaluated plans with declared resources; no original artwork is included.

src/services/renderer/programmatic/mv-type-card-renderer.ts adapts the quiet and
flicker Canvas composition from engine/scenes/typo.js at the same reference
commit. It draws Rust-evaluated typography, RGB/CRT slices, grain and light ramps
using explicitly declared project fonts, without original narrative defaults.

src/services/renderer/programmatic/mv-converge-renderer.ts rasterizes the typed
path, gradient and grain plans adapted from the convergence scene in
engine/scenes/intro.js at the same reference commit. Motion, beat selection,
noise and geometry are evaluated in Rust, not duplicated in the renderer.

src/services/renderer/programmatic/mv-ember-{raster,renderer}.ts replays the
typed light, shimmer, HUD and clipped-image plans adapted from the breathe,
ignite and collapse scenes in engine/scenes/intro.js at the same reference
commit. Scene timing, seeded motion and geometry remain in Rust; the browser
loads declared resources and supplies actual font/image facts.

